  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Reedy Creek is one of Charlotte's oldest and most-played courses — heavily wooded with wide fairways, creeks, and blind holes that have been testing locals since 1991. From the standard pins it plays a friendly 4,885 feet at par 55, but the trees make every shot a decision.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Dynamic Veteran baskets on moderately hilly ground, Reedy Creek is the kind of course that's approachable on paper and sneaky in the woods. The wide fairways forgive a little, the creeks don't.",
    "It's a staple of the Charlotte scene — the course where many of the city's best players took their first discs."
  ],
