  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 13 is the only par 4 at Reedy Creek — 378 feet that give the round its one true two-shot hole. From the tee it's a placed drive down a wide fairway; from there, a guarded approach to a basket the trees surround. It's the hole that breaks up the par 3 rhythm and the one that usually decides the round.",
  "localTips": "One of Charlotte's oldest courses — expect blind holes and creeks, so play the safe lines. The par 3s are the heart of the round; hole 13 is your one par 4 chance. Free to play, moderately hilly, and genuinely walkable.",
